From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] media: samsung: t715-camera: one media device per camera

What stays in t715-camera.ko is the capture side of one camera: CSIS,
FIMC-LITE and the PHY, programmed as proven on the device.  Each camera
is a media device; the sensor subdevice is found through the device tree
graph and linked to the video node.  The video node still exposes the
sensor's and the lens's controls, so the raw Photo and Selfie tools keep
working.

The sensors, their power, their mode tables and the focus motor moved to
VIDEO_T715_SENSOR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/Kconfig       |  13 +-
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/t715-camera.c | 804 ++++++++-----------
 2 files changed, 363 insertions(+), 454 deletions(-)

